@page "/case-study"

<SeoHead Title="Portfolio Case Study"
         Description="A factual private-beta LifeOS case study covering its local-first architecture, review boundaries and verified product surfaces."
         CanonicalPath="/case-study" />

<main class="page-shell">
    <section class="page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">PORTFOLIO CASE STUDY</p>
        <h1>A local-first operating system built around review and evidence.</h1>
        <p>
            LifeOS is in private beta. This case study describes verified
            behaviour and architecture without presenting future integrations as shipped.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-panel">
        <h2>Problem</h2>
        <p>Personal work, household, money and evidence become fragmented across tools and provider accounts.</p>
        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>Shared deterministic contracts, local storage, source provenance and explicit review gates connect those areas without hidden automation.</p>
        <h2>Result</h2>
        <p>A progressive desktop, Android and web product with repeatable tests, screenshot evidence and provider-neutral safety boundaries.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card"><h2>Desktop</h2><p>Deep administration, planning, review, audit and export.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><h2>Android</h2><p>Current workflows, offline state and explicit sync review.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><h2>Website</h2><p>Public documentation, onboarding, releases and factual portfolio packaging.</p></article>
    </section>
</main>
